# EMDR — git commit & push

## When the user asks to commit / push

If the user says **commit**, **push**, **commit push**, **ship**, or similar (any language, e.g. “uradi commit”, “pushaj”):

1. Follow the normal git safety protocol (status, diff, log; no force-push to main; no secrets).
2. **Hard gate before commit/push** (when code/config/behavior changed) — **required, never skip**:
   - `npm test`
   - `npm run lint` (ESLint via `next lint`)
   - `ReadLints` on files you touched in this turn
   - If **any** fail: fix first, re-run, then commit/push. **Do not push a red tree.**
   - **Do not** run `npm run build` / full Next compile before push — it slows the loop; GitHub Actions Docker build covers that. Lint + tests are enough locally to catch the errors that usually break CI.
3. **Commit** all relevant product/code/docs/rules changes from the current work in the same turn (include a rule/docs tweak made in that turn).
4. **Push** to the tracked remote (`git push -u origin HEAD` if needed) in the **same turn**, unless they explicitly said **commit only** / **bez push**.
5. Do **not** wait for a second confirmation after an explicit commit/push request.
6. After a coding session that changed files, if they say commit (even without “push”), treat it as **commit + push** — that is the default for this project.
7. If GitHub Actions fails after push, check whether it is **build** vs **Coolify deploy** (curl exit 22 / HTTP 401 = bad `COOLIFY_TOKEN`, not lint).

## After finishing work

Do **not** auto-commit without being asked.

When the user says commit/push after changes: ship immediately (commit + push) as above.

At the end of a coding turn (or when starting a new task), if **either** is true and they have not just asked to commit, briefly remind once:

1. **Many unpushed changes** — roughly **8+** modified/untracked product files, or a large diff vs `origin/main`, and nothing pushed yet for that work; or
2. **Stale push** — local commits ahead of `origin`, or substantial dirty tree, and the latest `origin/main` tip is older than about **1 day** (or this chat has shipped several features without a push).

Reminder tone: one short line, e.g. “Imamo dosta lokalnih izmena / nije bilo push-a odavno — hoćeš commit + push?”

Skip the reminder if they just pushed, or the only leftovers are noise (`.next`, build info, scratch scripts).

## What not to commit

- `.env`, credentials, `node_modules`, `.next`, scratch `scripts/_tmp-*`, `*.tsbuildinfo`
- Do not update git config; do not `--force` to `main`/`master`
